        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "594b4edd-f890-50e8-acdb-273b52b00fba",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lowell George, Ian Hunter, Christopher Cross, Ringo Starr, Howard Jones, Roger Hodgson, Sheila E, Greg Lake, Mark Rivera\n- Bands: Little Feat, Mott the Hoople\n- Albums and Songs: Ride Like the Wind, Ringo Starr and Friends\n- Roles: singer-songwriters, guitarist, vocalist, songwriter, record producer\n\nFacts:\n- Lowell Thomas George was born on April 13, 1945, and he was an American songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, and record producer.\n- Ian Hunter Patterson was born on 3 June 1939, and he is a British singer-songwriter known as Ian Hunter.\n- Ian Hunter was the lead singer of the English rock band Mott the Hoople from the band's inception in 1969 to its dissolution in 1974.\n- Lowell George was the primary guitarist, vocalist, and songwriter for the rock band Little Feat.\n- Lowell George died on June 29, 1979.\n- Christopher Cross dedicated the song \"Ride Like the Wind\" to Lowell George on the album's inner sleeve after Lowell George had died in 1979.\n- Ian Hunter participated as lead singer of Mott the Hoople again during the band's reunions in 2009 and 2013.\n- The album \"Ringo Starr and Friends\" included Ringo Starr's friends Ian Hunter, Howard Jones, Roger Hodgson, Sheila E, Greg Lake, and Mark Rivera.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
